  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is a market?', 'Any place or system where buyers and sellers come together to exchange goods and services.', 1),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is the difference between a physical and an electronic market?', 'Physical markets are places where buyers and sellers meet face to face; electronic markets operate online.', 2),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is a dynamic market?', 'A market that changes rapidly because of innovation, changing tastes or new competitors.', 3),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'How has online retailing changed markets?', 'It has increased competition, price transparency and convenience, and reduced barriers to entry, but hit high-street retailers.', 4),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is a competitive advantage?', 'A feature that allows a business to outperform rivals, e.g. lower costs, a strong brand or unique products.', 5),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is product differentiation?', 'Making a product distinctive from competitors'' through design, quality, branding or features.', 6),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is adding value?', 'Increasing the difference between the cost of inputs and the price customers are willing to pay, e.g. through branding, convenience or quality.', 7),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'How is market growth calculated?', '(Change in market size ÷ original market size) × 100.', 8),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is a sample in market research?', 'A group of people selected from the target population to represent it in research.', 9),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is random sampling?', 'Every member of the population has an equal chance of being selected.', 10),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is quota sampling?', 'Selecting a set number of respondents from each segment of the population, e.g. by age or gender.', 11),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is sampling bias?', 'When the sample doesn''t represent the population, leading to inaccurate results.', 12),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is a focus group?', 'A small group discussion led by a facilitator to gather qualitative views on a product or idea.', 13),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is a questionnaire''s main limitation?', 'Respondents may give inaccurate or biased answers, and poorly designed questions lead to misleading data.', 14),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is the role of ICT in market research?', 'Online surveys, social media analytics and loyalty card data make research faster, cheaper and more detailed.', 15),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is big data in market research?', 'Very large data sets from online activity and transactions, analysed to identify customer patterns and trends.', 16),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is demographic segmentation?', 'Dividing a market by characteristics such as age, gender, income and family size.', 17),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is geographic segmentation?', 'Dividing a market by location, e.g. region, country or urban/rural.', 18),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is psychographic segmentation?', 'Dividing a market by lifestyle, personality, values and interests.', 19),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What is behavioural segmentation?', 'Dividing a market by buying behaviour, e.g. usage rate, brand loyalty and occasion.', 20),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What are the benefits of market orientation?', 'Products meet customer needs, so demand is higher and the firm can respond to market changes.', 21),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.1', 'Meeting Customer Needs', 'What are the benefits of product orientation?', 'It can lead to innovative, high-quality products and technological breakthroughs.', 22),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What is demand?', 'The quantity of a good or service that consumers are willing and able to buy at a given price over a period.', 1),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What factors shift the demand curve?', 'Changes in income, tastes, prices of substitutes and complements, advertising, population and seasonality.', 2),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What is supply?', 'The quantity of a good or service that producers are willing and able to sell at a given price over a period.', 3),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What happens to equilibrium when supply increases?', 'The equilibrium price falls and the equilibrium quantity rises.', 4),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What happens to equilibrium when demand falls?', 'Both the equilibrium price and quantity fall.', 5),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What is excess demand?', 'When quantity demanded exceeds quantity supplied at the current price, putting upward pressure on price.', 6),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What is excess supply?', 'When quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded, putting downward pressure on price.', 7),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What does a PED of −0.5 mean?', 'Demand is price-inelastic: a 10% rise in price leads to a 5% fall in quantity demanded.', 8),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What does a PED of −2 mean?', 'Demand is price-elastic: a 10% rise in price leads to a 20% fall in quantity demanded.', 9),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'Why should a firm with inelastic demand raise prices?', 'The percentage fall in quantity demanded is smaller than the percentage rise in price, so total revenue increases.', 10),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'Why should a firm with elastic demand cut prices?', 'The percentage rise in quantity demanded exceeds the percentage fall in price, so revenue increases.', 11),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What does a positive YED of more than 1 mean?', 'The product is a luxury (income-elastic): demand rises proportionately more than income.', 12),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What does a YED between 0 and 1 mean?', 'The product is a normal necessity: demand rises less than proportionately with income.', 13),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What does a negative YED mean?', 'The product is an inferior good: demand falls as income rises.', 14),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'Why is YED important for businesses?', 'It helps predict how demand will change during booms and recessions, informing production and marketing plans.', 15),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What factors influence YED?', 'Whether the product is a necessity or luxury, and the proportion of income spent on it.', 16),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What is the effect of an indirect tax on supply?', 'It raises producers'' costs, shifting the supply curve to the left, raising price and reducing quantity.', 17),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What is the effect of a subsidy on supply?', 'It lowers producers'' costs, shifting supply to the right, lowering price and increasing quantity.', 18),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'Why do weather conditions affect supply?', 'They affect the output of agricultural products, e.g. poor harvests reduce supply.', 19),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'How does technology affect supply?', 'New technology usually lowers costs and increases productivity, shifting supply to the right.', 20),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'How can a firm make demand for its product more inelastic?', 'Branding, differentiation, building customer loyalty and reducing the availability of substitutes.', 21),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.2', 'The Market', 'What are the limitations of using PED?', 'It is hard to calculate accurately, it changes over time, and it assumes other factors stay constant.', 22),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is the marketing mix?', 'The 4Ps: product, price, place and promotion (7Ps for services add people, process and physical evidence).', 1),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What are the elements of the design mix?', 'Function, aesthetics and economic manufacture (cost).', 2),
