  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is psychological pricing?', 'Setting prices that appear lower, e.g. £9.99 instead of £10.', 12),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is competitive pricing?', 'Setting prices based on those charged by competitors.', 13),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is multichannel distribution?', 'Selling through several channels, e.g. shops, website and apps.', 14),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is a retailer?', 'A business that sells products directly to consumers.', 15),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is a wholesaler?', 'A business that buys in bulk from manufacturers and sells in smaller quantities to retailers.', 16),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is a question mark in the Boston Matrix?', 'A product with low market share in a high-growth market, needing investment to grow.', 17),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is a star in the Boston Matrix?', 'A product with high market share in a high-growth market.', 18),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is a cash cow?', 'A product with high market share in a low-growth market, generating cash to fund other products.', 19),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is a dog in the Boston Matrix?', 'A product with low market share in a low-growth market, often discontinued.', 20),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is marketing strategy for a mass market?', 'Wide distribution, mass media promotion, competitive pricing and a standardised product.', 21),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Marketing Mix & Strategy', 'What is marketing strategy for a niche market?', 'Targeted promotion, specialist distribution, premium pricing and a differentiated product.', 22),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Managing People', 'What is workforce planning?', 'Predicting the future number and skills of workers a business needs and planning how to meet them.', 1),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.4', 'Managing People', 'What is a part-time worker?', 'An employee who works fewer hours than full-time staff.', 2),
