  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Entrepreneurs & Leaders', 'What is a barrier to entrepreneurship?', 'Lack of finance, fear of failure, lack of skills, and regulation.', 19),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Entrepreneurs & Leaders', 'What is the role of government in supporting entrepreneurs?', 'Grants, loans, tax reliefs, advice, and reducing regulation.', 20),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Entrepreneurs & Leaders', 'What is business survival?', 'The ability of a business to continue operating, which is the main objective for many new businesses.', 21),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '1.5', 'Entrepreneurs & Leaders', 'Why might an entrepreneur find it hard to delegate?', 'They may be reluctant to give up control of the business they created.', 22),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is retained profit?', 'Profit kept in the business after tax and dividends, used for investment.', 1),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is sale of assets as a source of finance?', 'Selling assets such as property or machinery the business no longer needs to raise cash.', 2),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is a bank loan?', 'A sum of money borrowed for a fixed period with interest.', 3),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is a mortgage?', 'A long-term loan secured on property.', 4),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is share capital?', 'Finance raised by selling shares in the company.', 5),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What are the advantages of share capital?', 'No interest payments, and it doesn''t need to be repaid.', 6),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What are the disadvantages of share capital?', 'Loss of control and dividends expected by shareholders.', 7),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is a business angel?', 'A wealthy individual who invests in small businesses in return for equity and often provides advice.', 8),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is crowdfunding?', 'Raising money from many people, usually online.', 9),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is peer-to-peer lending?', 'Borrowing money directly from individuals through an online platform.', 10),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is leasing?', 'Renting assets such as vehicles and equipment rather than buying them.', 11),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is trade credit?', 'An agreement with suppliers to pay for goods at a later date.', 12),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is a government grant?', 'Money given by the government that doesn''t have to be repaid, often to support small businesses or particular areas.', 13),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is an overdraft?', 'A flexible short-term borrowing facility on a bank account.', 14),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is the difference between short-term and long-term finance?', 'Short-term finance is for day-to-day needs (overdrafts, trade credit); long-term finance is for investment (loans, shares).', 15),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is the purpose of a business plan?', 'It sets out the objectives, strategies and financial forecasts, helping to raise finance and guide decisions.', 16),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What does a business plan include?', 'The business idea, market research, marketing plan, financial forecasts and management team.', 17),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is a cash-flow forecast?', 'A prediction of cash inflows and outflows over a period.', 18),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is net cash flow?', 'Cash inflows minus cash outflows in a period.', 19),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What is the closing balance?', 'Opening balance plus net cash flow.', 20),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'Why are cash-flow forecasts useful?', 'They identify periods of cash shortage so the business can arrange finance in advance.', 21),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Raising Finance', 'What are the limitations of cash-flow forecasts?', 'They rely on estimates that may be inaccurate, and external changes can make them outdated.', 22),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is a sales forecast?', 'A prediction of future sales based on past data, market research and trends.', 1),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What factors affect sales forecasts?', 'Consumer trends, economic changes, and competitors'' actions.', 2),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is sales volume?', 'The number of units sold.', 3),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is sales revenue?', 'Price × quantity sold.', 4),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is total cost?', 'Fixed costs + variable costs.', 5),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is a fixed cost?', 'A cost that doesn''t change with output, e.g. rent.', 6),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is a variable cost?', 'A cost that changes directly with output, e.g. raw materials.', 7),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is contribution per unit?', 'Selling price − variable cost per unit.', 8),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is total contribution?', 'Contribution per unit × number of units sold, or total revenue − total variable costs.', 9),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is the break-even output formula?', 'Fixed costs ÷ contribution per unit.', 10),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is profit using contribution?', 'Total contribution − fixed costs.', 11),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What is the margin of safety?', 'Actual output − break-even output.', 12),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What happens to break-even if fixed costs rise?', 'The break-even point increases.', 13),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What happens to break-even if price rises?', 'Contribution per unit rises, so break-even output falls.', 14),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Financial Planning', 'What are the benefits of break-even analysis?', 'It is simple, shows the output needed to cover costs, and helps set targets and assess risk.', 15),
